            <ArticleTitle>Darkened skin, vomiting, and salt cravings in a teenager · Dx?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E1-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Acute adrenal insufficiency crisis usually occurs after a prolonged period of nonspecific complaints due to a loss of both glucocorticoids and mineralocorticoids; by the time overt symptoms occur, 90% of the adrenal gland may be destroyed. Patients (such as ours) may present with symptoms such as abdominal pain, weakness, vomiting, fever, and decreased responsiveness.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
